1. Make-whole spread. Our reading of the Applicable Premium definition is tha=
t, absent a Change of Control Triggering Event, any optional redemption prior=
 to the Par Call Date is priced at the discounted present value of remaining =
payments to the Par Call Date, using the Treasury Rate plus a make-whole spre=
ad of 50 basis points, floored at par. We understand the Par Call Date itself=
 to be 2030-06-15, one year ahead of the 2031-06-15 Stated Maturity.

2. Rating Event. Separately, we understand the Change of Control Triggering E=
vent definition to require BOTH (a) a Change of Control as defined, AND (b) a=
 Rating Event - and that a Rating Event is not satisfied by a decline from on=
ly one Rating Agency; the Indenture's own text requires a decline of at least=
 1 rating category from EACH of the Rating Agencies before the Rating Event c=
ondition is met. We would ask you to confirm this reading, since it is not ob=
vious on a first pass and has real consequences for how the put contingency s=
hould be modeled.

3. Rating Event trigger window. We further understand the relevant look-back/=
look-forward period to run 60 days from the relevant public-notice date, exte=
nded for so long as the rating remains under publicly announced review. Pleas=
e confirm this window is measured as we describe, since a shorter or differen=
tly-anchored window would change the answer materially.

We do not opine on the ultimate credit outcome and flag only the mechanics ab=
ove; we would appreciate your team's or the Trustee's confirmation before thi=
s is relied upon for planning purposes.

